-
name: The Neutral Zone
slug: 2026-10-neutralzone
date: 10 October 2026
venue: West Oxford Community Centre, Oxford, OX2 0BT
location: OXFORD
tagline: Something is spreading through the Neutral Zone...
description: |
  After thirty years of peace, how long can the Neutral Zone hold?
  
  The Alliance is a federation of planets that values exploration, diplomacy, and cooperation. The Dynasty is a feudal empire that values honour, strength, and loyalty to your House. A treaty ended their last war and created a demilitarised buffer zone between them - The Neutral Zone - into which neither side can send their Starships.
  
  Now there is something happening in the Zone, and pressure is mounting on both sides to step in.
  
  **This is a megagame**
  
  The Neutral Zone is a game for up to 42 players, split into teams of Bridge Officers on the Starships of the Alliance and Dynasty, each with faction, ship and personal goals. You'll negotiate with other players, deal with crises as they unfold, and make decisions that affect the whole map. There's no single winner; at the end of the day, your choices will have contributed to a shared story that nobody predicted at the start.
  
  *Due to safeguarding limitations, we unfortunately aren't able to accommodate players under the age of 18 at this game.*
tickets: https://www.tickettailor.com/events/7/2186972
listImage: images/neutralzone-list.png
bannerImage: images/neutralzone-banner.png
-
name: The Lighthouse
slug: 2026-09-lighthouse
date: 12 September 2026
venue: Quaker Meeting House, Reading, RG1 2SB
location: READING
tagline: There is a remote island that appears on no charts and has no name...
description: |
  If I were to vow at all, it should be to build a light-house (Benjamin Franklin)
  
  There is a remote island that appears on no charts and has no name. It is said that to travel there, you must steal a secret from the wind. It is said that travellers from other worlds can occasionally be met there. It is said that it hides great treasures, dark secrets, ancient gods, and unknown beasts. These things and many others are said, and some of them may even be true.
  
  On the island stands THE LIGHTHOUSE. By its beacon-glow, safe paths are found to places otherwise hidden from humankind, and indeed from many of the lesser spirits. The greatest of explorers eventually make their way here, and some of them eventually make their way back. That's you. Set out from THE LIGHTHOUSE on your voyages of discovery, and uncover secrets that will change the world forever.
  
  **This is a megagame**
  
  The game will last 5-6 hours, with 40-50 players all playing at once. You'll usually be part of a team of 3: either the explorers taking passage from THE LIGHTHOUSE; the wealthy patrons who fund their missions; or the Keepers, the ancient order who care for THE LIGHTHOUSE and its visitors. Explorers will have a single briefing as a team; patrons and Keepers may have additional personal goals. You will have rivalries with other teams as you seek to secure the most ground-breaking discoveries. There are also many secrets to discover, which may well require you to re-evaluate your goals as the game goes on.
  
  The game is driven by simple trading mechanics and elements of puzzle-solving. There's also space for you to come up with creative solutions to problems - if there isn't a rule for the thing you want to do, we'll make one on the fly. Teams will need to make deals with each other, and a certain amount of deception or trickery may be involved in negotiations. Unlike many games, there's no single winner; many players can achieve their goals, and even for those who don't, their journey through the day forms part of the wider narrative.
  
  You'll be assigned a role in the run-up to the game - and you'll have the chance to let us know what sort of role you want. There's a range of roles from purely roleplay and negotiation to trading and puzzle-solving - with plenty of variety we'll aim to put you in the role that you'll find most fun.
  
  *Due to safeguarding limitations, we unfortunately aren't able to accommodate players under the age of 18 at this game.*
tickets: https://www.tickettailor.com/events/7/2175403
listImage: images/lighthouse-list.jpg
bannerImage: images/lighthouse-banner.jpg
-
name: Mirrorshades
slug: 2026-06-mirrorshades
date: 13 June 2026
venue: Quaker Meeting House, Reading, RG1 2SB
location: READING
tagline: Get your crew, and get running!
description: |
  **They might own the world, but no-one owns the Net...**
  
  It is the late 21st Century and life in the West Coast Sprawl is dominated by powerful mega-corporations. Yet on the street, rebellious punks, lit by blazing bright neon, search for another way to live. The world is about to change...and you will decide whether it is the mega-rich oligarchs or the neo-anarchists who come out on top.
  
  Mirrorshades is a megagame of classic cyberpunk, in the tradition of Neuromancer, Altered Carbon and Netrunner. In the game, players take on the roles of the megacorp leadership and the punks who both despise and serve them in a world of neon-drenched, 80s influenced, gaming fun!
  
  **This is a megagame**
  
  Mirrorshades is a game for around 50 players. You'll be part of a team of 4, either the executives of a megacorp, or a gang of street punks. You'll also have personal goals, which may cause some tension with your team, but there are no out-and-out traitor roles. You'll find that some other teams are natural allies for you, and others may rapidly become sworn enemies.
  
  The game has board game style rules that are simple to learn but will take time to master. There's also space for you to come up with creative solutions to problems - if there isn't a rule for the thing you want to do, we'll make one on the fly. A certain amount of deception and trickery may be necessary, but you'll also need to find people you can ally with if you're going to survive. Unlike many games, there's no single winner; many players can achieve their goals, and even for those who don't, their journey through the day forms part of the wider narrative.
  
  **Get your crew, and get running!**
  
  You'll be assigned a role in the run-up to the game - and you'll have the chance to let us know what sort of role you want. There's a range of roles from purely diplomatic and negotiation to primarily focusing on game mechanics - with plenty of variety we'll aim to put you in the role that you'll find most fun.
tickets: https://www.tickettailor.com/events/7/2038923
listImage: images/mirrorshades-list.jpg
bannerImage: images/mirrorshades-banner.jpg
-
name: Aftermath
slug: 2026-04-aftermath
date: 11 April 2026
venue: West Oxford Community Centre, Oxford, OX2 0BT
location: OXFORD
tagline: It's the end of the world as we know it...
description: |
  **It's the end of the world as we know it...**
  
  No-one knows for sure what happened. Most people just call it "the Event" - pronounced with a capital E. Whatever it was, it wiped out civilisation as we know it. The cities were hit hardest - but you were some of the lucky few who were far enough out, and made it through the first, brutal winter.
  
  Now it's spring again. You, and the survivors who now look to you for leadership and guidance, can safely roam further from your hard-won shelter, scavenging for supplies and seeing who else is out there. Perhaps this is your chance to rebuild civilisation - do better than what came before. Or perhaps this is your chance to finally leave a life of tedious responsibilities behind and just enjoy what's left.
  
  There are still a few remnants of the former government kicking around, as well. When the Event happened, they did their best to save as many people as possible - but their resources were quickly overwhelmed. Now, they need to work out what their role is in this new world.
  
  **This is a megagame**
  
  Aftermath is a game for around 40 players. You'll be part of a team of 3, responsible for the wellbeing of a handful of survivors. Within your team, you'll work together completely - but other survivors may be less helpful. You'll need to build relationships - tenuous at first - with the other survivors, showing them they need to take you seriously, but making alliances where you can.
  
  The game has simple, board game style rules, but also allows for you to come up with creative solutions to problems - if there isn't a rule for the thing you want to do, we'll make one on the fly. A certain amount of deception and trickery may be necessary, but you'll also need to find people you can work with all day. Unlike many games, there's no single winner; many players can achieve their goals, and even for those who don't, their journey through the day forms part of the wider narrative.
  
  **Tea, Biscuits, and the Apocalypse**
  
  You'll be assigned a role in the run-up to the game - and you'll have the chance to let us know what sort of role you want. Most roles in this game focus on negotiation and creative problem-solving, with some interaction with basic game mechanics.
tickets: https://www.tickettailor.com/events/7/1963141
listImage: images/aftermath-list.png
bannerImage: images/aftermath-banner.png
-
name: The Generalissimo is Dead
slug: 2026-02-generalissimo
date: 21 February 2026
venue: St Luke's Parish Hall, Reading, RG1 5LR
location: READING
tagline: Il Generalissimo is dead! How can the country go on?
description: |
  **Members of the People's Party of Yugenya, tragedy has struck.**
  
  The Generalissimo has kept the country together with an iron fist since the revolution. Beloved by the people, feared by his enemies and respected the world over. Now, tragedy has struck and Il Generalissimo is dead! How can the country go on? Who will lead the people?!?
  
  Heavily inspired by The Death of Stalin, the game is set in the 1980s. Stuck between East and West, Yugenya is an under-developed nation with vast natural resources. The Generalissimo used these resources to expand the revolutionary guard, build a navy and establish an air force. Critics would also say he channelled much of the wealth into paranoia-fuelled schemes against imagined foes.
  
  Secure the Generalissimo's legacy from other Party Members who don't understand it as well as you do, and prepare a bright future for the people of Yugenya!
  
  **This is a megagame**
  
  The Generalissimo is Dead is a game for around 40 players. You'll be part of a team of 3-6, responsible for running a key government function. You'll also have personal goals, which may put you wildly at odds with your team (if they find out about them). You'll need to negotiate and strategize with other players, and occasionally lie to them, to get things done.
  
  The game has simple, board game style rules, but also allows for you to come up with creative solutions to problems - if there isn't a rule for the thing you want to do, we'll make one on the fly. A certain amount of deception and trickery may be necessary, but you'll also need to find people you can work with all day. Unlike many games, there's no single winner; many players can achieve their goals, and even for those who don't, their journey through the day forms part of the wider narrative.
  
  **The Party must stand together**
  
  You'll be assigned a role in the run-up to the game - and you'll have the chance to let us know what sort of role you want. Most roles in this game focus on negotiation and scheming, with some interaction with basic game mechanics.
  
  *Due to safeguarding limitations, we unfortunately aren't able to accommodate players under the age of 18 at this game.*
tickets: https://www.tickettailor.com/events/7/1953383
