name: Red Planet Rising
slug: 2025-04-rpr
date: 19 April 2025
venue: West Oxford Community Centre, Oxford, OX2 0BT
location: OXFORD
tagline: The post-apocalyptic martian megagame
description: |
  **What will the future of Mars be? It's up to you to decide.**
  
  As the governments of Earth began to colonise the solar system in a somewhat distant future, they thought the conflicts of the past were behind them as this brand new future dawned. Instead they just expanded the reach of the conflict, destroying all they'd built in an instant. It is a century since then and those that survived in the Martian colony of the Mariner Valley have begun to look towards the future of Mars, from old world corporations who have believed in their own propaganda, to crashed warships that are still flying the old flags to those who have made it through sacrifice and spirit. Each have a view to what this new Mars should look like - will they succeed and bring a new golden age to Mars, or will the sins of the past repeat themselves yet again?
  
  **This is a megagame**
  
  Red Planet Rising is a game for around 36 players. You will be part of a team of 3 players, each with aligned objectives, and will negotiate and strategize with other teams to achieve your aims. The game has simple, board game style rules with space that encourages you to come up with your own creative solutions to problems - if there isn't a rule for what you want to do, we'll make one up on the fly. There will likely be a degree of deception and treachery, whether intentional or accidental, but you'll need to find people that you can rely on to rebuild Mars. Unlike most games, there's no single winner. Instead, you'll each pursue your own team's goals, and at the end of the game your journey will form part of a wider narrative.
  
  **Mariner City Welcomes You**
  
  You'll be assigned a role in the run-up to the game - and you'll have the chance to let us know what sort of role you want. Each team has the same structure of a team leadership role, a military commander role and a resource lead role. But each have the freedom to act as they need in the best interests of their team.
listImage: images/rpr-list.png
bannerImage: images/rpr-banner.png
-
name: The Real Heroes
slug: 2025-03-realheroes
date: 29 March 2025
venue: Friends' Meeting House, Reading, RG1 4SB
location: READING
tagline: Superheroes vs Supervillains.
description: |
  **Kaboom! Zap! Pow!**
  
  A few years back, superpowered individuals began popping up all over America. Many of their powers were trivial, even comical - the ability to power a single lightbulb, or discern the thoughts of petunias. But many had powers which made them much more dangerous than the average mortal - super-speed, super-strength, flight. While some tried to use these powers for good, many others simply took whatever opportunities arose. Now, super-crime is on the rise, and anyone with powers has a decision to make. Does great responsibility truly come with great power? Who will be the real heroes?
  
  **This is a megagame**
  
  The Real Heroes is a game for around 40 players. You'll start as part of a super-team of 3-5, with loosely aligned objectives, but you'll have your own objectives and plot threads to pursue, and you may well end up breaking and re-building teams during the day. The game has simple, board game style rules, but also allows for you to come up with creative solutions to problems - if there isn't a rule for the thing you want to do, we'll make one on the fly. A certain amount of deception and trickery may be necessary, but you'll also need to find people you can work with all day. Unlike many games, there's no single winner. Instead, you'll pursue personal goals, and at the end of the game your journey will form part of a wider narrative.
  
  **Secret Identities Abound**
  
  You'll be assigned a role in the run-up to the game - and you'll have the chance to let us know what sort of role you want. While everyone is a super-powered individual and interacts with the same set of game rules, some roles will be classic heroes, others will be morally grey anti-heroes, and there may even be some out-and-out villains in the mix.
listImage: images/realheroes-list.png
bannerImage: images/realheroes-banner.jpg
-
name: Running Hot
slug: 2025-02-runninghot
date: 22 February 2025
venue: St Luke's Parish Hall, Reading, RG1 5LR
location: READING
tagline: A pre-cyberpunk game of corporations and hackers.
description: |
  Can you avoid the cyberpunk dystopia - or will you be the one to create it?
  
  In the not-too-distant future, a failing UK government hopes to revitalise the economy by creating the nation's first corporate city - a zone with no regulations, where capital is king. Greedy mega-corporations quickly leap at the chance to re-shape the world in their image. But they aren't just competing with each other - they also have to reckon with the "punks", small gangs of tech geniuses who can break any firewall, infiltrate any facility. Some are for sale to the highest bidder, while others have their eyes on a greater goal. Together, what future will they create? Or will the whole experiment crash and burn?
  
  **This is a megagame**
  
  Running Hot is a game for around 40 players. You'll be part of a team of 3-5, with mostly aligned objectives, and will negotiate and strategize with other teams to get things done. The game has simple, board game style rules, but also allows for you to come up with creative solutions to problems - if there isn't a rule for the thing you want to do, we'll make one on the fly. A certain amount of deception and trickery may be necessary, but you'll also need to find people you can work with all day. Unlike many games, there's no single winner. Instead, you'll pursue personal goals, and at the end of the game your journey will form part of a wider narrative.
  
  **Welcome, citizen**
  
  You'll be assigned a role in the run-up to the game - and you'll have the chance to let us know what sort of role you want. The corporation teams have political, financial, research and security roles, while the punks will initially all be quite similar, but have more chance to shape their roles as the day proceeds.
listImage: images/runninghot-list.png
bannerImage: images/runninghot-banner.jpg
